{"skill":{"slug":"google-weather","displayName":"Google Weather"},"version":{"version":"1.3.0","createdAt":1774205682220,"changelog":"**Added unit system selection (metric/imperial) via environment variable**\n\n- Support for `GOOGLE_WEATHER_UNITS` environment variable to choose metric or imperial units.\n- Weather output now displays values (temperature, wind, etc.) in the selected unit system.\n- Documentation updated: details and example outputs for both metric and imperial modes.\n- No code changes required for unit switching—set the environment variable and restart.","changelogSource":"auto","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3898,"sha256":"be9c92be099fb9479fe1f8c51011523d116eaf7d0d64a28c5377006cb08dbaad","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"lib/weather_helper.py","size":12195,"sha256":"9177961f3ae2aadcd8dddc8c525e6161ae1afc90ffa2261e6f7dd3c7047f30c9","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2097,"sha256":"f31aa32ca796cdfa44709ff813b127b645232bc6b1d3b230f9148f4685d01863","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789032753675,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"12d7eb5302efa8bb76a026aa22a1adf50b09d9268bf92e2dd118ae5c5dd7fc3a","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/12d7eb5302efa8bb76a026aa22a1adf50b09d9268bf92e2dd118ae5c5dd7fc3a","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: google-weather\nVersion: 1.3.0\n\nThe skill is a standard integration for Google Weather and Geocoding APIs. The code in lib/weather_helper.py correctly handles API requests, environment variables for authentication, and data formatting without any signs of malicious intent, data exfiltration, or suspicious execution patterns.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161308376},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":72,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":5,"checkedAt":1789032753675},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This weather skill uses a Google API key to send requested locations to Google for weather and geocoding, which matches its stated purpose and is disclosed in the skill documentation.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Outbound calls to weather.googleapis.com and maps.googleapis.com and use of a Google API key are proportionate for this feature, but users should understand that location queries are sent to Google.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Setup is documented as enabling Google Weather and Geocoding APIs and providing a GOOGLE_API_KEY or related environment variable; there are no package installs, hooks, or hidden installation steps.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill allows exec and instructs running a local Python helper; that is broad authority, but the provided instructions are limited to weather commands and no unrelated command execution is present.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The inspected files show no file writes, persistent memory changes, scheduled tasks, services, privilege escalation, or tool modification.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifact consistently describes a Google Weather skill, and the helper only performs geocoding, current weather, forecast retrieval, and formatting for user-supplied locations.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable providing a Google API key and having the locations you ask about sent to Google for geocoding and weather lookup. Review API key restrictions and billing controls in Google Cloud before use.","findings":"[LP1] expected: The helper does use requests.get for Google Weather and Maps endpoints, but that network access is central to the stated Google Weather API purpose and the documentation names the required Google APIs and key.\n[SQP-3] expected: Hebrew condition labels and Israeli quick-location shortcuts are visible, but they are formatting and lookup conveniences, not hidden control flow or unrelated access; the skill also documents worldwide locations.\n[SQP-2] expected: User-provided locations are sent to Google Geocoding and Weather APIs, which is expected for this weather lookup design and substantially disclosed by the setup and supported-location sections.\n[SQP-2] expected: The helper reads GOOGLE_API_KEY, GOOGLE_WEATHER_API_KEY, or GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY from the environment and uses the selected key for Google API calls, matching the documented setup.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789032753675}}}}}